Common reasons:
1. Home directory protection
Many systems have additional protections on home directories. Check the exact permissions:
bashls -ld /home
ls -ld /home/h
ls -ld /home/h/code
All three need the execute bit (x) for "others" to allow Apache to traverse the path.
2. SELinux context (if enabled)
Even on Arch, if you have SELinux enabled, files need the correct security context. Check if SELinux is active:
bash getenforce




